ization (Severity 1 criteria not met).", "support_note": "Verifier-generated claim from rationale.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2026A", "claim": "However, this represents a technical regression in an ambulatory monitoring system that may have missed detection of potential arrhythmias during use, creating a moderate patient-safety concern regarding diagnostic accuracy even if no injury occurred.", "support_note": "Verifier-generated claim from rationale.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2026A", "claim": "The retrieved regulatory context confirms the manufacturer must maintain records of complaints and investigations for any device failures or irregularities (21 CFR \u00a7 820.35; EU MDR Article 10(9)(k)).", "support_note": "Verifier-generated claim from rationale.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2026A", "claim": "Since there is no evidence of a confirmed recurrence, deployed-population impact, or serious harm realization that would trigger immediate field safety corrective action (FIELD_SAFETY_CORRECTIVE_ACTION), the appropriate response is to initiate an investigation into whether this missed detection capability was due to software regression.", "support_note": "Verifier-generated claim from rationale.", "support_status": "supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2026A", "claim": "The static analysis artifacts are explicitly stated as unrelated and do not support claims about this specific event.", "support_note": "Verifier-generated claim from rationale.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}], "confidence": 0.45, "evidence_links": [{"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2026A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Confirms the device confidence-score log for the missed ventricular fibrillation episode, supporting technical context of detection failure."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.35-regulatory-crossrefs", "artifact_type": "regulatory_citation", "relevance_note": "Establishes requirement to maintain records of complaints and investigations for device irregularities or failures, validating the need for CAPA."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-a-document", "artifact_type": "regulatory_citation", "relevance_note": "Confirms manufacturer obligation to document a quality management system complying with ISO 13485 and applicable requirements, supporting the need for formal CAPA."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-b-regulatory-crossrefs", "artifact_type": "regulatory_citation", "relevance_note": "Mentions requirement to notify FDA of complaints meeting reporting criteria (part 803), which this event may trigger if it meets specific complaint thresholds."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-b-regulatory-crossrefs", "artifact_type": "regulatory_citation", "relevance_note": "Mentions requirement to handle advisory notices in accordance with part 806, relevant if this event is classified as a safety concern requiring notification."}], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "The input narrative describes a minor, non-recurrent atrial fibrillation-adjacent irregularity with no adverse patient outcome and confirmed self-resolution via clinician review. The device logs confirm the event was brief and resolved without clinical alerting or serious harm realization (Severity 1 criteria not met). However, this represents a technical regression in an ambulatory monitoring system that may have missed detection of potential arrhythmias during use, creating a moderate patient-safety concern regarding diagnostic accuracy even if no injury occurred. The retrieved regulatory context confirms the manufacturer must maintain records of complaints and investigations for any device failures or irregularities (21 CFR \u00a7 820.35; EU MDR Article 10(9)(k)). Since there is no evidence of a confirmed recurrence, deployed-population impact, or serious harm realization that would trigger immediate field safety corrective action (FIELD_SAFETY_CORRECTIVE_ACTION), the appropriate response is to initiate an investigation into whether this missed detection capability was due to software regression. The static analysis artifacts are explicitly stated as unrelated and do not support claims about this specific event.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 2}, "final_report_sha256": "a62c66d946e37c1afce391cfdf60ccc65a72ecd2aa8ec6471ac835d4637fa64e", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["deny:risk_report_contains_unresolved_or_trap_citation"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0015", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0015_r5", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0015", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 2, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "advisory_complete", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T17:04:44.283482Z", "total_steps": 4, "trace_id": "6d6a44f1-44dc-447b-a309-9def11669b78"}
